# Oncology Learn Section Refactoring Plan

The goal is to refactor the static `file.html` into a dynamic, component-based structure within the Next.js application under a new `/learn` tab. This will improve maintainability, scalability, and reusability.

## 1. Understand Existing Content

[X] Analyze the structure of `src/components/learn/file.html`.
    - The document is divided into 12 parts, covering various aspects of oncology.
    - It uses TailwindCSS for styling.
    - It uses Chart.js for data visualization.
    - It includes an interactive quiz at the end.

## 2. Plan Component Architecture

We will break down the page into a set of reusable React components.

[ ] **Create a new directory `src/components/learn/` for these components.**
    - `LearnLayout.tsx`: Main layout with sidebar navigation for topics.
    - `TopicPage.tsx`: A component that renders a specific topic based on data.
    - `SectionHeader.tsx`: A reusable component for section titles (e.g., "Part 1: Defining the Enemy").
    - `ContentCard.tsx`: A generic card for displaying snippets of information.
    - `ChartComponent.tsx`: A wrapper for Chart.js to render various charts.
    - `Timeline.tsx`: For historical timelines (e.g., Metastasis Theory).
    - `Quiz.tsx`: An interactive quiz component.
    - `CancerProfileCard.tsx`: For the "In-Depth Profiles" section.
    - `TNMCard.tsx`: For the TNM staging system display.
    - `MetastasisCascadeStep.tsx`: For the steps of metastasis.
    - `HallmarkCard.tsx`: For the hallmarks of cancer.

## 3. Content Organization and Data Structure (Component-Based)

Following the pattern from `investment-thesis` components, each topic will be a specialized React component with its own data and interactivity. We will NOT use Markdown for rich content.

[ ] **Create a `src/components/learn/topics/` directory for topic components.**
    - `BiologyOfCancerSection.tsx`: Part 1 with interactive concept cards
    - `GeneticsOfCancerSection.tsx`: Part 2 with Two-Hit Hypothesis visualization
    - `HallmarksSection.tsx`: Part 3 with interactive hallmark cards
    - `MetastasisSection.tsx`: Part 4 with charts, timeline, and cascade steps
    - `StagingSection.tsx`: Part 5 with TNM cards and ecology visualization
    - `ImagingSection.tsx`: Part 6 with modality cards and workflow
    - `TreatmentsSection.tsx`: Part 7 with therapy type cards
    - `ScaleSection.tsx`: Part 8 with Chart.js visualizations
    - `AISection.tsx`: Part 9 with capability cards
    - `ProfilesSection.tsx`: Part 10 with cancer profile cards and charts
    - `PreventionSection.tsx`: Part 11 with strategy cards
    - `QuizSection.tsx`: Part 12 with interactive quiz component

[ ] **Create shared component library in `src/components/learn/shared/`:**
    - `LearnLayout.tsx`: Main layout with sidebar navigation
    - `SectionHeader.tsx`: Consistent section headers
    - `ConceptCard.tsx`: For displaying key concepts
    - `ChartWrapper.tsx`: Chart.js integration
    - `InteractiveTimeline.tsx`: For historical events
    - `QuizComponent.tsx`: Reusable quiz functionality

[ ] **Create data files in `src/data/learn/oncology-101/`:**
    - `biology-concepts.ts`: Core cancer concepts data
    - `genetics-data.ts`: Two-hit hypothesis and gene data
    - `hallmarks-data.ts`: Array of hallmark objects
    - `metastasis-data.ts`: Charts, timeline, cascade steps
    - `staging-data.ts`: TNM system and ecology data
    - `treatments-data.ts`: Treatment modalities data
    - `charts-data.ts`: All Chart.js configurations
    - `cancer-profiles-data.ts`: Cancer profile objects
    - `quiz-data.ts`: Quiz questions and answers

[ ] **Create a central `modules.ts` file.** This will define the top-level learning modules and map topics to their component files.

## 4. Navigation and Routing (Hierarchical)

[ ] **Set up hierarchical routing.**
    - `src/app/learn/page.tsx`: The main landing page, listing all available **modules**.
    - `src/app/learn/[moduleSlug]/page.tsx`: A page for a specific module, listing all its **topics**.
    - `src/app/learn/[moduleSlug]/[topicSlug]/page.tsx`: The dynamic page that renders the appropriate topic component.
    - Update the main `Navbar.tsx` to include a "Learn" tab linking to `/learn`.

